name issue_124_burst_loss_v2
describe 3% loss in bursts of ~6 packets, 2 Mbps, every v2 switch on: the flip's burst_loss cell next to libwebrtc (issue #124)
# `burst_loss` with the configuration PR #116 makes the default. Measured on main 74266b3, seeds 1-10 (ours / libwebrtc, parity-data of main):
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 45-108 (mean 73.5) / 46.8 ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 188-241 (mean 210.7) / 213.0
#   cc.utilization_pct 81.1-87.0 (mean 84.0) / 80.4 ; cc.target_avg_kbps 1787 / 1757 ; video.freeze_total_ms 640 / 1433
# Issue #124 root cause: the test bench sent each 20 ms audio packet at t = 0 mod 20 ms, the phase of the 30 fps video
# frames; libwebrtc's harness sends it at 10 mod 20 (10 ms ADM blocks). Replayed open loop through our GoogCC, libwebrtc's
# packets give libwebrtc's overuse times; ours, with the old phase, gave later ones. With the libwebrtc phase, seeds 1-10:
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 33-63 (mean 45.0) / 46.8 ; cc.utilization_pct 79-84 (mean 82.4) / 80.4
# The lines below lock the level reached.
# Target (issue #124): cc.queue_p95_ms within the parity band of libwebrtc (46.8 ms).
cc v2
pacer v2
rtx v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2000kbps delay=50ms loss=3% burst=6 queue=300ms
expect audio.concealed_pct < 5
expect audio.interruptions <= 1
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 1200
expect video.render_fps >= 25
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 75
# Was < 260. Owner rule on PR #216 (program.md 0.2, 2026-10-20 23:11 UTC): just above our seed-1 value, never above
# libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10. Ours seed 1 304.4 (timing v2); the suggested < 330 is above libwebrtc's worst seed, so
# the bound is that seed's value. libwebrtc seeds 1-10: 305.95 304.60 296.60 243.00 239.25 236.72 288.35 314.08 285.63
# 236.00 (worst 314.08, mean 275.0).
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 314.08
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 78
